{
 "format": 1,
 "kind": "sweepercad-asset",
 "name": "Teapot",
 "notes": "A teapot in seven sweeps. The body is a circle swept up with its silhouette drawn as the scale graph; it is hollowed by a second sweep of the same kind, the wall thinner - note the cavity's graph is the silhouette re-mapped onto the cavity's own (shorter) spine, because the graph's x is the travel along the spine. The spout is a circle along an S-curve tapering by its graph, bored by the same sweep 2 mm thinner run from inside the belly out past the lip, so the pot really pours. The handle is a rounded rectangle along a C-curve with both ends sunk into the body; the foot is a ring (a circle on a circular spine). The lid - flange, dome, knob - is its own root so it lifts off. Fillets only on the two seams that show: spout and handle.",
 "graph": {
